      "**09/02/2026 05:57 — Mor Rasam?**\n\nYes 🙂 **Mor rasam** = **buttermilk rasam**. Light, cooling, stomach-friendly. Morning-perfect stuff.\n\nimage_group{\"query\":[\"mor rasam\",\"buttermilk rasam South Indian\",\"neer mor rasam\",\"curd rasam\"]}\n\n### 🥣 Simple Morning Mor Rasam (1 serving)\n\n**Ingredients**\n- Buttermilk (mor) – **250 ml** (thin, not thick)\n- Water – **100 ml**\n- Cumin (jeera) – **½ tsp** (crushed)\n- Green chilli – **½** (crushed) *(optional morning)*\n- Ginger – **½ tsp** (crushed)\n- Curry leaves – **6–8**\n- Turmeric – **1 pinch**\n- Salt – to taste\n\n**Tempering (optional but nice)**\n- Ghee – **½ tsp**\n- Mustard seeds – **¼ tsp**\n- Cumin – **¼ tsp**\n- Dry red chilli – **½**\n\n### 👩‍🍳 Method\n1. Mix **buttermilk + water + salt + turmeric**.\n2. Add **crushed jeera, ginger, green chilli, curry leaves**.\n3. Heat on **very low flame** → **DO NOT BOIL**.  \n   Stop when steam comes & aroma rises.\n4. Optional: do quick tempering in ghee, pour on top.\n5. Rest **2 minutes**, then drink.\n\n### 🌿 Morning Logic (why mor rasam)\n- Cooling (unlike pepper/tomato rasam)\n- Rehydrates gut after night fast\n- Gentle probiotics\n- No acidity spike\n\n### ❌ Morning avoid\n- Tomato\n- Pepper\n- Garlic (save for lunch rasam)\n- Heavy chilli\n\n### 🕖 Best time\n- **6:00–9:00 AM**, empty stomach or with kanji.\n\nIf you want, I’ll give you:\n- **Mor rasam ↔ tomato rasam ↔ pepper rasam weekly rotation**\n- Or **kanji + mor rasam combo ratio**  \n\nTell me 👍"
     ]
    },
