      "**10/02/2026 12:42 — Rasam timing rule (morning vs lunch vs night)**  \nLock this once and you’ll never second-guess rasam again 🔒\n\nimage_group{\"query\":[\"mor rasam\",\"tomato rasam\",\"pepper rasam South Indian\",\"garlic rasam\"]}\n\n---\n\n## 🌅 MORNING RASAM (5–9 AM)\n**Purpose:** Wake digestion gently, cool gut\n\n**Base**\n- Buttermilk (mor) + water\n\n**Use**\n- Jeera (whole or powder)\n- Ginger\n- *Tiny* green chilli (optional)\n- Curry leaves\n- Turmeric, salt\n\n**Avoid**\n- ❌ Tomato  \n- ❌ Pepper  \n- ❌ Garlic  \n- ❌ Heavy chilli  \n- ❌ Boiling\n\n**Heat**\n- Very low flame → steam only\n\n**Tempering**\n- ❌ Not needed  \n- Optional: ¼ tsp ghee *after* switching off\n\n👉 This is **drinkable rasam**, not rice rasam.\n\n---\n\n## ☀️ LUNCH RASAM (12–2 PM)\n**Purpose:** Proper digestion for heavy meals\n\n**Base**\n- Tomato + water (or tamarind-light)\n\n**Use**\n- Jeera\n- Pepper\n- Garlic (2–3 cloves)\n- Red chilli\n- Curry leaves, coriander\n\n**Heat**\n- Proper boil (2–3 mins simmer)\n\n**Tempering**\n- ✅ Must (ghee/oil)\n  - Mustard + jeera + dry chilli\n\n👉 This is **rice rasam**. Strong is good.\n\n---\n\n## 🌙 NIGHT RASAM (7–9 PM)\n**Purpose:** Gas relief, light cleanse, sleep-friendly\n\n**Base**\n- Water or very thin tomato (optional)\n\n**Use**\n- Jeera\n- Pepper (less)\n- Ginger\n- Garlic (1 small clove optional)\n\n**Avoid**\n- ❌ Too much chilli  \n- ❌ Very sour tomato/tamarind\n\n**Heat**\n- Gentle simmer, not aggressive boil\n\n**Tempering**\n- Optional, very light\n\n👉 Sip slowly. Small quantity only.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 ONE-LINE MEMORY TRICK\n- **Morning = Mor (cool)**\n- **Lunch = Tomato + spice (strong)**\n- **Night = Pepper/jeera (light)**\n\nIf you want next:\n- **Weekly rasam rotation chart**\n- **Rasam ↔ curd ↔ kanji timing rules**\n- **Marriage food logic (why curd + rasam together works)**"
     ]
