    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "**05:59 — No, you do NOT need to temper in ghee.**  \nNot crushing is **totally fine** for **morning mor rasam** 👍\n\n### Here’s the clean rule (lock this 🔒)\n\n#### ❌ Morning (now)\n- **No ghee tempering needed**\n- Add **raw jeera + ginger + green chilli directly**\n- Heat gently → aroma releases on low flame\n- Result: **light, cooling, gut-safe**\n\n#### ✅ When tempering IS useful\n- Lunch / dinner rasam\n- When using **pepper, garlic, tomato**\n- When rasam is meant to be **stimulating**\n\n### Why no temper now\n- Ghee + heat = heavier digestion at 6am\n- Raw additions + low heat = gentle extraction\n- Buttermilk already carries flavour well\n\n### If you *really* want extra aroma (optional)\n- After switching off, add **¼ tsp ghee** on top  \n- **No frying**, just melt-and-drink\n\nBut honestly?  \n👉 **Skip tempering now. You’re doing it right.**  \nWarm, not hot. Slow sips. Done 🌿"
     ]
