    },
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Perfect 👍 you’re actually **fully set**.\n\n### 05:59 quick mor rasam (using jeera + ginger + green chilli)\n\nimage_group{\"query\":[\"mor rasam\",\"buttermilk rasam South Indian\",\"neer mor rasam\"]}\n\n**Ingredients**\n- Buttermilk – **250 ml**\n- Water – **100 ml**\n- Jeera – **½ tsp**\n- Ginger – **½ tsp**\n- Green chilli – **½** (or less)\n- Curry leaves – **6–8** (tear by hand)\n- Turmeric – **1 pinch**\n- Salt – to taste\n\n**What to do (no crusher needed)**\n1. **Just tear / break by hand**:\n   - Split green chilli\n   - Roughly break ginger\n   - Lightly rub jeera between fingers\n2. Add everything to buttermilk + water.\n3. Heat on **very low flame**.\n4. Stop when:\n   - Steam rises  \n   - Smell comes  \n   - **Before boiling**\n5. Switch off, rest **1–2 min**, drink.\n\n### Tiny tip (important)\n- If it starts bubbling → immediately off.\n- Morning mor rasam should feel **warm**, not hot.\n\n### Why this combo works\n- Jeera → digestion\n- Ginger → gas control\n- Green chilli → mild wake-up, not heat\n- Buttermilk → cooling base\n\nYou’re doing it exactly right for this hour 🌅  \nIf you want, next I can lock a **morning vs lunch vs night rasam rule** so no confusion ever again."
     ]
    },
